WEBVTT

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.820
<b>Episode 5  "Hunter"</b>

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.820
A smartphone?

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.900
<i>The cuffs are about to unlock.</i>

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.550
<i>Please take your interface.</i>

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.870
<i>I will now explain the third program.</i>

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.940
<i>You currently have 100 points.</i>

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.830
<i>Please collect 1,000 points.</i>

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:54.880
<i>That is all!</i>

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.650
That's it?!

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.760
No explanation about this thing?

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.210
Wind?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.250
I'm outside?!

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.830
<i>The time is now 1:18 PM.</i>

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.320
<i>For the next thirty minutes,</i>

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.490
<i>every person knocked out in 
Block A is worth ten points.</i>

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.490
<i>Please begin!</i>

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.340
<i>This has to be Block A.</i>

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.840
<i>Do I stay here, or keep moving?</i>

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.990
<i>No question—I run!</i>

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.270
<i>One thousand points is the goal.</i>

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.140
<i>Ten points per person in 30 
minutes is a trivial amount.</i>

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.000
<i>This is likely an ongoing game.</i>

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:45.820
<i>And I think others have entered the 
third program ahead of us!</i>

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.670
<i>I still don't have a feel 
for how this program works.</i>

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.020
<i>I'm at an immense disadvantage.</i>

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.730
Lucky me!

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.150
I'm the first one here.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.050
<i>They know where we come out?</i>

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.020
<i>I don't have a choice.</i>

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.780
<i>I'll have to strike first—</i>

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.800
H-Hold it!

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.690
Hear me out, won't ya?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.250
I'm not here to fight ya.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.780
You set up an ambush, 
but you don't want to fight?

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.620
That seems unlikely.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.730
But that really isn't why I'm here!

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.590
I'm here to recruit ya!

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.060
Recruit?

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.990
Get away from me, you damned perverts!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:35.940
Yuuri?!

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.140
Akira!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.190
What happened? Are you all right?

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.940
Do I look all right?!

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.870
You see that bunch of creeps right there?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:51.070
Damn... How'd that girl get so fast?

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.660
This is bad news...

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.750
It's Red's quartet of fools!

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.140
You're one of the Green brats, ain't you?

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.000
You on a recruitin' mission, too?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.530
Lucky me!

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:07.240
We can snag two at once! 
The boss'll be pleased as punch!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.480
I've got a good feeling about this!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:15.600
<b>Dragon</b>

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.100
Hey, you kids!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.690
You see this intimidating "Dragon" symbol?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.650
We're the notorious...

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.140
...hoodlums...

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.360
...of Team Red!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.080
The Red Dragon Team!

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.180
That's us!

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.740
<b>Dragon</b>

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:25.700
<b>DRGN</b>

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.660
<b>Draguhn</b>

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.560
At least coordinate your symbols.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.890
Hey, Green boy!

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.710
Hand those two over to us!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.200
If you do, we might just let you go!

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.630
Mitsuru! W-We're gonna get two girls!

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.640
I've got a good feeling about this!

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.910
Kaji! How stupid are you?

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.830
That one's a man!

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.310
He's in a man's uniform!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.260
What?!

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.000
Is this true, Matsushita?!

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.400
Is that a man?

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:59.300
Girls in men's uniforms are hot as hell!

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.930
But the shoulder width and 
build suggest "male."

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:06.060
If Perv Matsushita says it, I believe it.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:09.470
There's no hiding such things 
from a connoisseur like myself!

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:13.270
It just speaks to me!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.280
Enough!

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.240
It's time for Red Dragon's...

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.930
ultimate combo!

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.720
Moonflower Profusion!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.710
<b>Moonflower
Profusion</b>

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.670
You won't survive this one!

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.130
Listen up, Greenie...

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.500
If you think you can fight us, 
you got another thing comin'.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.920
Be a good boy and—

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.400
<b><<Hunter>>

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.790
You—

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:47.030
Ya think I'd sell these kids 
to Red to save myself?!

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.830
I'll buy ya time to run away.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.260
I can't let the Reds have ya,
 no matter what.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.220
Matsushita!

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.210
Your wish is my command!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.040
That's—

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.250
Trés bien!

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.290
A-Akira! He's got your—

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.170
I think you guys know how this cannon works!

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.650
He's got your cannon!

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:17.810
There's no escape from the ultimate abi—

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.030
<i>Your</i> cannon?

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.480
<i>The ultimate ability?</i>

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.480
Yes.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.290
I also...

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.460
<i>That's very interesting.</i>

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.980
...have the cannon ability.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.340
<i>Yes! I can use it!</i>

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.450
That little brat!

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:49.670
Can't believe he's got a cannon!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.360
We gotta grab him!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.380
If we don't—

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.400
Now!

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.750
Damn you!

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.350
Matsushita! Shoot that brat!

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.640
I was hoping you'd try that!

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:26.950
I can't believe he shot Matsushita's shot!

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:29.330
Th-They got away!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.310
They can't have gone far! After them!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.450
Matsushita?!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.760
Don't tell me that explosion got you?

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.950
I-I'm such a failure...

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.410
I-I'm chickening out!

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.240
You great fool!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.380
I don't wanna fight 
without Matsushita! It's scary!

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.730
We let the cannon kid get away.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.870
Who's gonna tell the boss about this?

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:18.080
You saved me, but I haven't even 
introduced myself, let alone said thanks.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.340
I'm Katsuya Saitou.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.210
You don't need to thank us.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.210
You tried to save us first, after all.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:30.190
Those men wanted to drag 
us away against our will.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.960
It seems clear that they 
meant to do us harm.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:40.500
In response, you didn't hesitate to show 
your ability and fight to protect us.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.140
"Protect anyone—ally or not—from the Reds."

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:46.950
Is that your philosophy... 
the Greens' philosophy?

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.510
Our names are Akira Shiroyanagi 
and Yuuri Amagake.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.770
We're the ones who should be thanking you.

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:55.750
So, thanks.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.010
<i>Who is this kid?</i>

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.520
Say, what's all this "Reds" 
and "Greens" stuff, anyway?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.140
It's a bunch of factions.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.180
Most people play the third program in teams.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.610
I'm a Green.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.950
Those guys were Team Red.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.470
They're no joke.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:19.620
They're led by two guys with 
crazy abilities and sharp minds.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.070
That reminds me...

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.000
You said something about 
recruiting us earlier.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:28.920
Will you take me to Team Green?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.650
Hey, Katsuya!

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.030
You managed to get some recruits?

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.510
I did, Shima!

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.400
I want to take them to meet the big man.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.710
Come on in, then!

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:41.380
Welcome back.

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.710
Amazing!

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.460
It almost looks like...

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.980
...a village.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.500
Katsu!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.070
Hey, Hareka!

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.680
I made it back.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.780
Being a good boy, Taro?

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.530
A baby?

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.820
How'd they get a baby here?

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.240
Look.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.470
No cuffs.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.100
Yeah.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.070
Taro was born here.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:19.550
His mother was three months 
pregnant when she arrived.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:23.130
Taro's mother does work with her ability,

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.440
so I'm looking after him while she's gone.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.640
Want to hold him?

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.620
You bet I do!

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.150
Pregnant women, children, old people...

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.230
He's so heavy!

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:34.310
We don't turn anyone away.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.710
That's the reason ya wanted 
to come here, right?

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:43.480
<i>This program is different 
from the first two.</i>

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.130
<i>What in the world happened?</i>

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.130
Be back later!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:45.880
Sure!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.050
This is our meeting room.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.680
It's the core of our base.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.390
Our leader will explain it all to ya.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.960
Just wait here.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.460
I guess we meet again...

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.650
Pretty quick reunion, huh?

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:16.670
Indeed.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.820
After that emotional goodbye! 
It's really kinda crappy.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.270
Yeah, you said it.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:35.290
But I would have sought you out, 
so I'm glad you came to me.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:42.270
The people here seem pretty nice.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.310
That's why you chose to come, right?

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.790
Not just that, I'm afraid.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:52.160
From what I can tell about 
the third program so far,

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.020
it shouldn't be possible 
to take care of the weak.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:59.920
The fact that they can afford to do 
that suggests they're very strong.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:05.560
They've created a base this large and kept
 up their team while taking on all comers.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:10.500
They must have multiple members 
with superlative abilities.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.520
<i>And a leader who can make that happen...</i>

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:17.560
<i>I think this team is a good 
fit for me in this program.</i>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.380
Come on in.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.610
A pleasure to meet you.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.250
I'm Shirasagi, this team's leader.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:35.390
I heard that you saved Katsuya's life.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.830
Let me thank you for that.

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:38.640
Not at all.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.260
He's the one who saved us.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:40.960
Yeah.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.800
I'm sure you've been through 
a lot, but you'll be safe here.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.990
And... Akira Shiroyanagi, was it?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:50.030
I'm told you're interested 
in learning about our team.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.460
And your ability is the cannon?

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:55.530
We'll be very glad to have you!

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:59.080
We've been lacking in powerful 
abilities like yours!

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:04.720
Hey! You said they had lots 
of superlative abilities!

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.020
Buh?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:09.310
By the way, Yuuri, what's your ability?

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.880
Me?

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.070
You're joining us too, right?

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.270
I'd love to hear, if ya don't mind.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:21.560
It's the "quintuple your 
physical abilities" one.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.020
Wh-What did you say?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.370
I said, the "quintuple your 
physical abilities" one.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.310
Wh-What?!

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.310
W-Well...

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:41.000
Abilities like the cannon one are 
considered top-notch A-class abilities,

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:46.960
but the quintuple one is super ultra rare,
 ranked even higher at A+ class!

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.780
F-For real?

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:51.710
<i>Well, it is kind of game-breaking.</i>

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:54.380
Katsuya!

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:58.090
You brought us a cannon and a quintuple!

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:00.150
This could change everything!

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.790
It could completely turn the tables!

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:06.110
You did such a good job, Katsuya!

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:12.750
E-Excuse me.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.530
I lost my head for a moment.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.920
I'm sure you have a number of questions.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:26.900
I'll start by explaining 
the situation we're in.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:32.410
The key to the third program is the 
points collected in these interfaces.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.810
Points are earned by completing quests 
assigned by the organization.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.310
The points are like currency.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.510
We can pay them to the organization 
to buy various things.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:45.530
<b><i>Point Exchange</i></b>

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:47.430
What kinds of things?

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:51.950
Food, medical supplies, refills of
 things our abilities use...

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.500
Even valuable information!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:59.170
Live here, complete quests, 
and aim for a thousand points.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.950
That's the third program's basic concept.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:07.770
When I first got here, everyone was 
forming teams of single-digit members.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:12.290
Small groups are highly mobile, 
and nobody fights over point distributions.

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.360
So it just ends up that way.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:17.570
But eventually,

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:22.890
I began to hear of a team rapidly expanding 
its membership into the dozens.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:25.370
I thought it was strange,

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:27.800
but we were busy with our 
own problems, so I paid it no mind.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.650
But eventually an unsettling 
rumor began to spread.

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:37.570
The large team was kidnapping people 
for reasons outside of quests.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:39.780
Yuuri...

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:43.240
I'm talking about Team Red, 
the ones that attacked you.

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:44.750
Those guys...

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.780
But they're not getting 
any points for it, right?

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:48.970
So why...

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:51.790
Why do you think, Akira?

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:56.510
Team Red has no intention of 
moving on to the next program.

00:15:56.920 --> 00:15:58.100
Is that it?

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.290
Precisely.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:04.390
This isn't a place anyone 
wants to stay for long,

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:08.360
but there's no guarantee that the 
next program will be any better.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:12.040
At the very least, if you have a 
powerful ability and enough points,

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.790
you can purchase materials.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:18.760
And so Team Red has begun to 
use their ability advantage

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.640
to make this world into their own kingdom.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:28.150
To make a life here as kings, 
exploiting those with weak abilities...

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:29.710
They decided that was their best scenario.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.330
I'm s-so sorry...

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:38.560
I'm told the four of you together 
let a new kid get away...

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:41.680
<b>Team Red Leader: Hajime Oogami</b>

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.310
And one with a cannon, at that.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:44.400
Y-Yes... Well...

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.080
We actually...

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.930
<i>What's that chick doin' here?</i>

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:50.370
That's all right.

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.640
We have his face and his name.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:58.060
It's not as if a cannon or two 
will turn the tables now.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:16:59.690
Rin...

00:17:00.340 --> 00:17:02.510
Let them have a beer, too.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:07.090
Come and get it.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:09.050
S-Sure...

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.180
Th-Thanks...

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:22.630
I told you that I'd kill you 
if you failed to catch them.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:28.260
That's enough, Ichi.

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:31.750
I told you, I don't mind

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:35.450
<b>Team Red Sub-Leader: Masaya Kuroiwa</b>

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:35.130
if you discipline the men, 
but try not to make such a mess.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.680
Oh, get off my back already.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:39.660
It's not harming you, Kuro.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.510
Oh, but it is.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:44.630
If one drop of blood gets 
on my clothing or shoes,

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:46.760
I'll kill him on the spot.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.050
Take that garbage out of here.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:51.200
It's in the way.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:56.060
So what do we do about the cannon kid?

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:59.570
You're right that the cannon is irrelevant.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:06.060
But I am curious about how a newcomer kid 
managed to escape from our little quartet.

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:10.650
That brat... There's more to 
him than just the cannon.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.660
More?

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.610
<b>Akira Shiroyanagi</b>

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.610
<b>16 Years Old</b>

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.610
<b>Ability:         Cannon +α?</b>

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.620
There seems to be a large 
influx of extras today.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:22.570
Ichi, if one of them has 
a rare ability like yours...

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:26.380
And they were to team up 
with someone like me...

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:29.050
That <i>would</i> demand our attention.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:39.750
Team Red exploits the weak 
and uses them like slaves.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:42.220
Exploits the weak...

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:50.450
I couldn't abide their tyranny any longer.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:54.500
That's why, in order to protect the weak,

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.050
we created a force in 
opposition to Team Red.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.320
Is that Team Green?

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.140
Yes.

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:03.030
And there's one other team...

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.070
They have their individual 
objectives and styles,

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:10.610
and declare neutrality in the conflict so 
that both Green and Red leave them alone.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:12.370
We call them Team Blue.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.650
Team Red, which hunts others,

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.970
Team Green, which opposes them,

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.110
and Team Blue, which is neutral...

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:26.350
The third program is currently 
divided into those three factions.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:31.020
We're going to fight Team Red sooner or later.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.120
We need you two.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.700
I want you to fight with us.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:39.590
I'll do it.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:44.320
If these Team Red guys really 
are doing that awful stuff...

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.910
I'm gonna crush them!

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.620
And what about you, Akira?

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:56.120
You're already in conflict 
with the Red Dragons,

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:00.620
and if you were the kind of man to 
go Blue, you wouldn't be here right now.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.340
I don't think you have a choice.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:05.300
You'll join, won't you, Akira?

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:10.760
<i>But I don't want to join because 
I don't have a choice.</i>

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.140
<i>I want to </i>choose this place, 
and have a reason to do it.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.310
<i>But I do have a choice, don't I?</i>

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:26.730
Akira!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.680
Neither of you move.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:31.410
If you move, he'll shoot.

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:34.210
I see...

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:39.100
You do have the choice... 
to take me hostage.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:43.060
That would open up quite 
a few options for you.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:45.520
But is that what you want?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.410
<i>Impossible.</i>

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:50.510
<i>The cannon's not appearing!</i>

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:54.500
<i>It should activate under these conditions.</i>

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:58.450
<i>Does their leader have an ability that 
prevents abilities from activating?</i>

00:20:58.450 --> 00:20:59.400
<i>Or...</i>

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:01.140
<i>Is it possible?</i>

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:05.830
<i>He's not entirely convinced that 
I have the cannon ability?</i>

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.900
Put your hand down, Akira!

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:09.790
Why are you doing this?

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.710
Oh, it really is the cannon.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.730
Ready to see where this takes you?

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:26.310
Fire, and you might learn 
what you want to know.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:39.900
<b><<Hunter>>

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:12.780
<b>Mion and Yang's 
\h\h\hNext Episode Preview</b>

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:12.780
Mion and Yang's Next Episode Preview!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:15.790
Did you enjoy the fifth episode 
of <i>Battle Game in 5 Seconds</i>?

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:18.050
Wait a minute! That's supposed 
to be your line, Yang!

00:23:18.050 --> 00:23:20.600
I don't think you're going to 
take the preview seriously!

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.540
Oh, I've learned my lesson.

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:25.950
I heard that last week, 
"#MionDoThePreview!" was trending!

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:27.340
I don't think that happened.

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.350
But I'm glad you've learned your lesson!

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:32.380
Okay! Time for Mion and Yang's 
Next Episode Preview!

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:32.930
Okay!

00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.230
Oh no! We're down to five seconds!

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:35.800
Hurry, Yang! Hurry!

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:39.450
S-See you next time! Oh, not again!
